# Rule 12 allowlist (see xtask/src/legacyrule.rs and ADR-0022 section 8): every use of a legacy
# presentation API that is still allowed, with the exact number of uses, the date the row expires
# and the M22b slice that deletes the use together with its legacy path.
#
#   ban | file | uses | expires (YYYY-MM-DD) | deleting slice
#
# The list only shrinks. A new row, a higher count or an expiry past 2026-12-12 is not allowed;
# when a slice deletes a use it lowers or removes the row in the same commit (the rule fails on a
# stale count). A row past its expiry fails CI: delete the path, do not extend the date. Dates are
# the cut-over plan of docs/reports/m22b1-plan.md; moving one needs a docs/decisions.md row.
#
# Counts come from `cargo xtask legacy --print`. Test code is not scanned (it is deleted with the
# path it exercises).



